{{Quote|Corellian-hound tamers are crazy. Even with their padded clothing and protective gloves, they are still in biting range of those terrible teeth!|An [[unidentified artist]] in [[Unidentified artist's journal|his journal]]|<ref name="Alien Archive" />}}
'''Corellian hounds''' were a [[species]] of [[Dog|hound]] from the [[planet]] [[Corellia]] with many breeds including the white '''Sibian'''. They were quick and nimble canines used by locals for a number of tasks. Due to their keen sense of smell, they were often used for [[hunting]] and tracking. They had a vicious bark and bite, which meant they could be quite effective for protection and criminal gangs were fond of using the hounds for defense or to attack their rivals. Corellian hounds were also present on the planet [[Ushruu]], where they were known as '''snarlers''', and the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] planet of [[Ferrix]], where they were referred to as '''Ferrix hounds'''.{{Fact}}

==Biology and appearance==
[[File:CorellianHound-SoloUSC.png|thumb|left|200px|A profile view of a Corellian hound.]]
Corellian hounds were a [[species]] of [[Dog|hound]] from the [[planet]] [[Corellia]]. They were fast<ref name="SoloOG" /> and nimble<ref name="Alien Archive" /> and had an excellent sense of smell<ref name="SoloOG" /> and a viscous bite.<ref name="Alien Archive" /> Various breeds of the hounds were used across Corellia<ref name="SoloOG" /> for various tasks<ref name="Alien Archive" /> and adapted to various environments<ref name="UltimateSW" /> and they were later spread further across [[the galaxy]].<ref name="SWECG">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref> They were often bred for [[hunting]] and tracking or attack and protection due to their bites and intimidating barks<ref name="Alien Archive" /> and were seen as formidable opponents.<ref name="Bestiary">''[[Star Wars Bestiary, Vol. 1: Creatures of the Galaxy]]''</ref> One of the most popular Corellian breeds was the Sibian which had white skin, orange [[eye]]s, regenerating [[Tooth|teeth]] and a sturdy set of<ref name="Alien Archive" /> white [[bone]]-like scales along the crest of their heads along to their shoulders<ref name="UltimateSW" /> called an osteoderm plate ridge. They also had three<ref name="SoloOG" /> bony<ref name="Squadrons">''[[Star Wars: Squadrons]]''</ref> spiked tendrils protruding from their cheeks underneath their eyes.<ref name="Bestiary" /> Some Corellian hounds were 0.7 [[meter]]s (2 [[Foot|ft]] 4 [[List of measurement units#Length|in]]) tall. The Sibians were prone to fighting and due to their savage bites often lost some of their regenerating teeth.<ref name="UltimateSW" /> A variation of the Sibian with grey skin also existed.<ref name="Andor 1" />

==Corellian hounds in the galaxy==
{{Quote|Beeta, Serenata, Sibak. At ready.|[[Prybolt Garavult]]|<ref name="The High Republic: Midnight Horizon">''[[The High Republic: Midnight Horizon]]''</ref>}}
[[File:CorellianHoundSkull-Squadrons-cropped.png|thumb|right|200px|Skull of a Corellian hound, used as an ornament in a [[TIE/ln space superiority starfighter|TIE]] cockpit]]
Taming of Corellian hounds was seen as notoriously difficult<ref name="Squadrons" /> and dangerous and tamers often used protective [[clothing]] and [[glove]]s.<ref name="Alien Archive" /> Corellian hounds, especially Sibians, were often employed by criminal gangs as guards, attack-dogs, and trackers.<ref name="UltimateSW" />

During the [[Imperial Era]], the [[White Worms]] gang of [[Lady]] [[Proxima]] on Corellia kept a pack of<ref name="Solo" /> four<ref name="SWcom">{{SW|url=news/creature-feature-5-things-you-might-not-know-about-corellian-hounds|text=Creature Feature: 5 Things You Might Not Know About Corellian Hounds}}</ref> Sibian Corellian hounds.<ref name="Solo" /> By [[13 BBY]],<ref name="Solo-Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of the prologue of ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]'' to [[13 BBY]].</ref> they were handled by the older thugs [[Rebolt]] and [[Syke]], the favorite goons of their leader [[Moloch]]. Rebolt was the more experienced of the two handlers<ref name="SoloOG" /> and rough to his animals,<ref name="UltimateSW" /> while still sometimes spoiling them with biscuits which were better than the food of most of the [[scrumrat]]s to mock them, and used the threatening and valuable hounds leverage his position within the gang.<ref name="SWcom" /> Meanwhile Syke, who was quickly catching up to his rival, was more gentle and fond to the hounds which Rebolt saw as a weakness to exploit. Syke had a favorite hound, named [[Taomat]], which he hoped to someday set on his rival.<ref name="SoloOG" /> The fourteen year old scrumrat [[Ema]] had scars from when she had been attacked by the hounds before joining the gang.<ref name="CrimsonClimb">''[[Crimson Climb]]''</ref> In 13 BBY,<ref name="Solo-Date" /> Moloch, Rebolt and Syke used two of the Sibian hounds to track the deserted members [[Han Solo|Han]] and [[Qi'ra]]; first transporting them in their<ref name="Solo" /> [[A-A4B truckspeeder]]<ref name="SoloOG" /> and then using them to track them during the ensuing foot chase through the streets and the [[Coronet City Spaceport]].<ref name="Solo" />

A group of Corellian 'junkyard' hounds were kept by the [[human]] [[Pegla]], the de facto head of security at [[Zorby's Western Shiplot]]<ref name="DB Pegla">{{Databank|pegla|Pegla}}</ref> on the [[planet]] [[Ferrix]], to protect the shipyard from trespassers. At some point on an early morning in [[5 BBY]], the dogs were running on the [[Rix Road]], passing<ref name="Andor 1" /> the [[B2 groundmech]]<ref name="SWECG" /> [[B2EMO]], as one of them stopped and [[urine|peed]] on the [[droid]], causing it to be shocked by him.<ref name="Andor 1" /> Later that year,<ref name="AndorDate2">{{AndorDate|112}}</ref> Pegla and his hounds guarded the [[Caleen Salyard]] to watch it until it was sold.<ref name="RixRoad-EG">{{SW|url=series/andor/andor-season-1-episode-12-episode-guide|text="Rix Road" Episode Guide &#124; Andor}}</ref>

Natives of the planet [[Ushruu]] referred to the hounds as snarlers.<ref name="Forest of Fear!">''[[The Mighty Chewbacca in the Forest of Fear!]]''</ref><ref name="Bestiary" />

Around [[34 ABY]],<ref name="GE date">The events of [[Dok-Ondar's Den of Antiquities]] within [[Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge|''Star Wars'': Galaxy's Edge]] take place in [[34 ABY]], per ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''.</ref> [[Dok-Ondar]] had the head of a Corellian hound mounted on the wall of his [[Dok-Ondar's Den of Antiquities|store]] on [[Batuu]]. The plaque the head was mounted on had the words "In memory of [[Yay Jakk|Yay-Jakk]]" painted on it in [[Aurebesh]].<ref name="Galaxy'sEdge">{{GalaxysEdge|Dok-Ondar's Den of Antiquities}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|They [the dogs] loved it so much they actually put their own prosthetic heads on. All you had to do was hold the creature head, and they walked up and put their heads in it.|Neal Scanlan on the dog actors|<ref name="ArtofSolo">''[[The Art of Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref>}}
Corellian hounds were first featured in the [[2018]] [[Star Wars Anthology Series|''Star Wars'' Anthology]] film ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''.<ref name="Solo" /> The hounds had been present in the film since the first draft of the script, and according to co-writer [[Jon Kasdan]] were his tribute to the Death Dogs from [[Lucasfilm]]'s [[1988]] film [[Willow (film)|''Willow'']], which had scared terrified him as a child.<ref name="Jon Kasdan">{{Twitter|JonKasdan|status/994087163506683904|[[Jon Kasdan]]|quote=In a bizarre TWIST OF FATE, these #CorellianHounds, which were in the script from the very first draft, were 100% a loving homage to the DEATH DOGS in @RealRonHoward 's WILLOW, which terrified me as a kid, particularly when they mauled that poor nursemaid.}}</ref> ''Willow'' was coincidentally also directed by ''Solo''{{'s}} later director [[Ron Howard]].<ref name="SWcom" />

The Corellian hounds were designed by [[Martin Rezard]]. Among the different concept designs was also one by [[Jake Lunt Davies]] of a realistic dog with black fur wearing a muzzle with green lights which he described as "a touch of [[Wikipedia:Gorilla|gorilla]] mixed with some hard tech".<ref name="SWcom" /> Rezard created at least seventeen alternate designs, multiple of which incorporated<ref name="ArtofSolo" /><ref name="Rezard">{{WebCite|url=https://martinrezard.com|text=martin rezard|work=[[Martin Rezard]]'s website|archivedate=20250412182843}}</ref> [[Wikipedia:Warthog|warthog]]-like<ref name="SWcom" /> fur and big tusks, multiple with [[armor]] or [[cybernetics]], multiple with [[Reptile|reptilian]] features, one with a [[Wikipedia:Lion|lion]]-like mane, and multiple with red skin.<ref name="ArtofSolo" /><ref name="Rezard" /> The production titles of the different designs included "Dog", "Hell Dogz", "Robot Dog" and "[[Wikipedia:Piranha|Piranha]]". The reasoning behind the hound's white skin was that they would spent most of their in the dark of the [[Den of the White Worms]] and as such had less pigments in their skin similar to Proxima and the other [[Grindalid]]s. Rezard also created a<ref name="ArtofSolo" /> clay sculpt of the design using a scan of a dog as a basis.<ref name="Rezard" /> Creature supervisor [[Neal Scanlan]], who had been inspired by [[Mardji]], the [[Wikipedia:Asia elephant|Asian elephant]] who played two [[bantha]]s in the original [[1977]] ''[[Star Wars]]'' film, [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']], suggested to use real [[Wikipedia:Dog|dogs]] in prosthetics for the creatures, which was seen as a crazy idea.<ref name="ArtofSolo" />

On set they were they were played by four dogs, two [[Wikipedia:Dobermann|Dobermanns]] named [[Blackie (dog)|Blackie]] and [[Boyce (dog)|Boyce]], and two [[Wikipedia:Northern Inuits|Northern Inuits]] named [[Saxon (dog)|Saxon]] and [[Elsa (dog)|Elsa]] in specially made costumes fabricated by [[Sherri Hazzard]] and [[Laura Sindall]]<ref name="SWcom" /> and "artworked" by [[Henrik Svensson]].<ref name="Rezard-IG">{{Instagram|username=martin_rezard|name=[[Martin Rezard]]|url=p/Bm-xGC-g9_s|date=2018-08-27|quote=Corelian hounds dog suits, for Solo, fabricated by sherry hazzard and laura sindall, artworked by henrik svensson, designed and sculpted by myself,🐶}}</ref> The dogs were slowly trained for the role for months<ref name="SWcom" /> in multiple little steps by animal trainer [[Jo Vaughan]]<ref name="SWShow">{{StarWarsShow|GSw6uIumxaU|Star Wars Jedi: Fallen Order Announced, Exploring the World of Corellia, and Author Claudia Gray!|sw_url=video/star-wars-jedi-fallen-order-announced-exploring-the-world-of-corellia-and-author-claudia-gray}}</ref> and were said to be happy in their roles and to have liked the costumes. Neal Scanlan said that he liked the unpredictable movements the dogs would sometimes make during their scenes that would have been forgotten by puppeteers or animators, but helped the hounds come over more realistically animal like.<ref name="ArtofSolo" /> During post production, the faces of the dogs' suits were animated to make them move realistically, the dogs' feet were painted over, and their tails,<ref name="MakingofSolo">''[[Industrial Light & Magic Presents: Making Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> which had been wrapped in green fabric,<ref name="SWShow" /> were also painted out.<ref name="MakingofSolo" /> The production team also created multiple automated puppets,<ref name="SWcom" /> built by [[Christopher Clarke]],<ref name="Rezard" /> and rod puppets of the hounds which were used for some scenes<ref name="SWcom" /> including close ups<ref name="MakingofSolo" /> and the scenes inside the speeder, where they were puppeteered by [[Brian Herring]] and [[Colin Purves]].<ref name="SWcom" /> Due to the combination of different techniques, the Corellian hounds were a favorite on set.<ref name="MakingofSolo" />

The Corellian hounds later returned for the [[Andor Season 1|first season]] of the television series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'', released in [[2022]],<ref name="Andor 1" /> where they were once again portrayed by real dogs in suits.<ref name="RixRoad-EG" /> [[Toby Haynes]], the director of the first three episodes said that he really enjoyed the scene with the hounds and B2EMO.<ref name="Career Highlight">{{WebCite|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-features/andor-episode-8-toby-haynes-forest-whitaker-stellan-skarsgard-1235250954|text=‘Andor' Director Toby Haynes Talks That Forest Whitaker-Stellan Skarsgard Scene: “It Was a Career Highlight”|author=Davids, Brian|date=2022-10-28|archivedate=20221029050743}}</ref>

===LEGO===
[[File:TanayHounds-LSW140.jpg|thumb|left|200px|Tanay hounds in ''Droids, Troopers, and Snakes. Oh My!'']]
A breed of the hounds with brown skin appears in "[[Droids, Troopers, and Snakes. Oh My!]]," a comic featured in the magazine [[LEGO Star Wars 140|''LEGO Star Wars'' 140]] written by [[Martin Fisher]] and published on [[May 29]], [[2026]]. A pair of hounds chase after [[Luke Skywalker]], who is searching for a [[holocron]] on the [[jungle]] [[planet]] [[Tanay]].

===Inconsistencies===
While they actually are a distinct breed of Corellian hound,<ref name="Alien Archive" /> many sources conflate the Sibians with the overall species<ref name="DB">{{Databank|corellian-hounds|Corellian hounds}}</ref><ref name="SWcom" /><ref name="Bestiary" /> or are otherwise unprecise about the distinction.<ref name="SoloOG" /><ref name="UltimateSW" /><ref name="SWECG" />

