{{Quote|You look strong enough to pull the ears off a gundark.|[[Han Solo]], to [[Luke Skywalker]]|audio=EarsOffAGundark.flac|<ref name="Episode 5">{{Film|V}}</ref>}}
'''Gundarks''' were vicious [[Diet|carnivorous]] [[desert]] [[mammal]]s from the planet [[Vanqor]]. Renowned for their power and ferocity,<ref name="VE" /> the large creatures had sixteen claws<ref name="Absolutely Everything">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> and keen hearing.<ref name="Lost Gundark" /> To tell someone that they "looked strong enough to pull the ears off a gundark" meant that they were healthy and strong.<ref name="Episode 5" />

At some point prior to [[Anakin Skywalker]] and [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]]'s assignment of guarding Senator [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] from an assassination attempt, Obi-Wan and Anakin fell into a gundarks' nest, although Anakin reminded Obi-Wan that he went in the nest to rescue Obi-Wan.<ref name="Episode II">{{Film|II}}</ref> The gang leader [[Tasu Leech]] used a gundark bone as [["Huttsplitter" blaster rifle|his rifle's]] grip.<ref name="TFAVD">''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref>

A group of gundarks were present in [[Lexim's hunting ground]] on a [[Unidentified planet (Lexim)|forest planet]].<ref name="Becoming Hunted">{{RebelsMagCite|10|Becoming Hunted}}</ref>

==History==
{{Quote| I haven't felt you this tense since&hellip; since we fell into that nest of gundarks.''"<br />"''You fell into that nightmare, Master, and I rescued you. Remember?''"<br />"''Oh&hellip; yes.|Obi-Wan Kenobi and Anakin Skywalker|<ref name="Episode II" />}}
During [[Anakin Skywalker]]'s apprenticeship under [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], Kenobi fell into a nest of gundarks. However, Skywalker was able to rescue him from the nest.<ref name="Episode II" /> During the [[Clone Wars]], Kenobi and Skywalker [[Skirmish at Vanqor|pursued]] Count [[Dooku]] to Vanqor. After Dooku escaped, they were then confronted by one. Skywalker was chased by one, until Kenobi knocked it unconscious. The gundark was sealed in a cave by Skywalker's Padawan, [[Ahsoka Tano]], as well as several [[clone trooper]]s.<ref name="Dooku Captured" />

After the Jedi Cruiser ''[[Endurance]]'' [[Sabotage of the Endurance|crash-landed]] on Vanqor, Skywalker and [[Mace Windu]], along with [[R2-D2]] and [[R8-B7]] went to examine the crash site for survivors. Unfortunately, a pair of gundarks attacked the two astromechs and R8 was torn apart. As the gundarks attempted to do the same to R2, a bomb went off and killed one of the gundarks. R2 tried to send off a distress signal to Coruscant using [[Anakin Skywalker's Delta-7B Aethersprite-class light interceptor|Skywalker's interceptor]], but was forced to tie a gundark to it in order to pull it away.<ref name="R2 Come Home">{{TCW|R2 Come Home}}</ref>

A [[Ming Po]] animal trainer used two gundarks to battle Windu on [[Zardossa Stix]]. With help from [[Jar Jar Binks]], Windu succeeded in killing one gundark, while the surviving gundark fled.<ref name="Disappeared 2">{{TCW|The Disappeared, Part II}}</ref>

[[Trandoshan]]s, such as [[Garnac]] and members of his [[Garnac's hunting guild|hunting guild]], would hunt gundarks, skin them for their pelts and put them on display.<ref name="Padawan Lost">{{TCW|Padawan Lost}}</ref> 

The criminal leader [[Skraik]] had a pet gundark named [[Gigi (Gundark)|Gigi]]. He abused her with a shock stick and when he was deposed as leader of his [[Skraik's gang|gang]], Gigi took the shock stick and attacked Skraik with it.<ref name="The Size of the Fight">{{RebelsMagCite|29|The Size of the Fight}}</ref>

[[Lor San Tekka]] wore a [[belt]] made of gundark hide.<ref name="TFAVD" /> [[Zorii Bliss]] wore [[glove]]s from the same material.<ref name="TROS VD">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref>

{{Creature-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Gundarks were first mentioned in [[Star Wars: Episode V The Empire Strikes Back|''Star Wars'': Episode V ''The Empire Strikes Back'']],<ref name="Episode 5" /> though they did not appear in [[canon]] until the first season of the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' television series, in the episode "[[Dooku Captured]]."<ref name="Dooku Captured" /> Their first appearance in any ''[[Star Wars]]'' media was in the 1981 Marvel comic [[Star Wars (1977) 51|''Star Wars'' (1977) 51]].<ref name="SW 1977">[[Star Wars (1977) 51|''Star Wars'' (1977) 51]]</ref>

