'''Kaadu''' were creatures native and indigenous to the [[planet]] [[Naboo]]. During a [[Battle of Naboo|fight]] on the [[Great Grass Plains]], kaadu were deployed with [[fambaa]]s to support the [[Gungan Grand Army]] to fight off the [[Trade Federation]] [[battle droid]]s.<ref name="TPM" /> Kaadu were raised as livestock for [[Smoked Kaadu Ribs|consumption]] by some residents of the planet [[Batuu]].<ref name="GEStaff">[[Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge|''Star Wars'': Galaxy's Edge]] has official backstory elements that, though not directly published for the public, are officially canon details that can be obtained verbally from cast members working in the land.</ref> They possessed a keen sense of hearing.<ref name="Big & Small">''[[Star Wars: Creatures Big & Small]]''</ref> Gungans considered taming a kaadu to be a sign of reaching adulthood.<ref name="TVE" />

==Biology and appearance==
The kaadu was a two-legged [[reptavian]] that had great strength and endurance. They were swift and agile creatures that possessed sharp hearing and a keen sense of smell.<ref name="TPM" /> They had long legs and sleek hides that helped them move swiftly on land and in [[water]].<ref name="Absolutely Everything">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> Kaadu came in shades of yellow and bright oranges. The area around their [[eye]]s was a periwinkle color. The kaadu were primarily land dwellers, but they were also capable of breathing underwater for extended periods of [[time]].<ref name="TPM" /> They could be found in single-[[gender]] flocks of no more than 100 individual kaadu.<ref name="bestiary" /> A kaadu mother laid 6 to 8 [[egg]]s.<ref name="Absolutely Everything" />

==History==
[[File:WelcomeBackJarJar-TPM.png|thumb|300px|left|Gunga City Guards rode kaadu while patrolling the city.]]
For generations, the [[Gungan]]s domesticated kaadu to use as steeds for traveling through the swamps and [[forest]]s. The kaadu were respected by the Gungans for their strength, endurance, and loyalty. It became common for Gungans to decorate their kaadu with giant feathers. The [[Gungan Grand Army]] came to rely on them as mounts for their patrols<ref name="TPM" /> and the [[Gunga City Guard]] used them to patrol [[Otoh Gunga]].<ref name="SWU">{{SWU|set=Homeworlds|cardname=Gunga City Guard|link=1446255223}}</ref>

During the [[Battle of Naboo]] in [[32 BBY]],<ref name="SWGA">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> kaadu and [[fambaa]]s were deployed onto the [[Great Grass Plains]] to support the Gungan Grand Army to fight off the [[Trade Federation]] [[battle droid]]s.<ref name="TPM" />

Some residents of the planet Batuu raised kaadu for [[Smoked Kaadu Ribs|consumption]].<ref name="GEStaff" /> In 34 ABY,<ref name="GEdate">''[[Galaxy's Edge: Black Spire]]'' starts concurrent with the [[Battle of Takodana]] and the [[Hosnian Cataclysm]], which are depicted in [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|Star Wars: Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']], then jumps four [[Standard month|months]] ahead to the [[Resistance]] establishing its presence on [[Batuu]], and concludes with an epilogue set several [[Standard week|weeks]] later, when the [[First Order]] occupies the [[planet]] and the [[Battle of Batuu]] begins. The themed land [[Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge|''Star Wars'': Galaxy's Edge]] is set during the occupation and depicts the Battle of Batuu via the attraction [[Star Wars: Rise of the Resistance|''Star Wars'': ''Rise of the Resistance'']]. ''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]'' dates the battle to six months after the events of ''The Force Awakens'', which are dated by ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas|Star Wars Galactic Atlas]]'' to [[34 ABY]]. Furthermore, ''[[The Star Wars Book]]'' dates the Battle of Batuu to 34 [[Standard year|years]] after the end of [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV A New Hope]], which ''Star Wars: Galactic Atlas'' dates to [[0 ABY]]; this again places the Battle of Batuu in 34 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|ABY]]. Therefore everything within Galaxy's Edge and any related [[Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge (media project)|media]] depicting the Battle of Batuu, or set between ''The Force Awakens'' and the battle, must take place in that year.</ref> smoked kaadu ribs were served at [[Docking Bay 7 Food and Cargo]] at [[Black Spire Outpost]] on [[Batuu]].<ref name="GEStaff" />

==Behind the scenes==
Originally, the kaadu were to be native [[Tatooine]] beasts of burden.<ref name="DB">{{DB|creature|eopie|eopie}}</ref> However, due to the evolving story of [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']], which called for the Gungans to be beast-riding soldiers, the kaadu was transported to Naboo,<ref name="DB2">{{DB|creature|kaadu|kaadu}}</ref> and the [[eopie]] was created in its place from modified concept art of the kaadu.<ref name="DB" /> Upon their transfer to Naboo, the kaadu were given aquatic characteristics, particularly a duck-billed snout and smoother skin.<ref name="DB2" />

Kaadu snorts were created by slowing down a mixture of pig noises with the sound of whales spouting water through their blowhole.<ref name="Absolutely Everything" /><ref name="Scenes">''[[Star Wars in 100 Scenes]]''</ref>

''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]'' and ''[[Star Wars Bestiary, Vol. 1: Creatures of the Galaxy]]'' classifies kaadu as [[reptavian]]s, while ''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]'' and the [[Databank (2014-)|Databank]] say they are [[Bird|avians]]. As the species has more reptavian than avian traits, this article uses the former classification.

