{{Quote|After seeing this creature in action, I have come to the conclusion that I am not a cat person.|An artist, in his journal|<ref name="Alien Archive" />}}
'''Nexu''' were predatory [[feline]]s [[Homeworld|native]] to the [[planet]] [[Cholganna]].<ref name="UFC" /> They were also found on [[Zhanox]],<ref name="Uprising">''[[Star Wars: Uprising]]''&mdash;Crew Run: "Excavator Repairs"</ref> [[Vodran]],<ref name="Join the Resistance">''[[Join the Resistance]]''</ref> and [[Saleucami]].<ref name="Cut and Run">{{TBB|Cut and Run}}</ref>

==Biology and appearance==
{{Quote|But if you're going ''after'' those responsible for my friend's death&mdash;then please take the ''nexu''. Seems she already has taken a ''liking'' to you&hellip;or she would've eaten you by now.|[[Furball]]'s trainer, to [[T'onga]] and [[Losha Tarkon]]|<ref name="Bounty Hunters 10">[[Bounty Hunters 10|''Bounty Hunters'' 10]]</ref>}}
[[File:Bestial_Fury_SM.png|thumb|left|250px|A nexu in the wild on Cholganna]]
Nexu were agile catlike animal predators with four<ref name="UFC" /> [[Color|red]] [[eye]]s<ref name="AotC" /> and a defensive mane<ref name="VE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref> of sharp quills.<ref name="UFC" /> The four eyes gave them excellent vision, with the second pair allowing them to track prey by its body heat<ref name="VE" /> using [[infrared]] vision.<ref name="SW:AEYNtK" /> The nexu was 4.51 [[meter]]s long and typically 0.94 meters tall.<ref name="SWE" /> Nexu possessed sharp [[Tooth|teeth]] and long claws, perfect for climbing [[tree]]s. Their double tails were forked and [[Whip (disambiguation)|whip]]-like.<ref name="VE" /> A nexu's light build allowed it to remain highly agile and difficult to hit, but also meant that it was easily hurt or even killed if struck with enough force; a single kick was enough to stun a nexu and cause significant pain.<ref name="AotC" /> In contrast, a nexu's hide did seem durable enough to withstand [[blaster]] fire.<ref name="Cut and Run">{{TBB|Cut and Run}}</ref>

Despite their ferocity, it was possible to tame and train a nexu.<ref name="Bounty Hunters 4">[[Bounty Hunters 4|''Bounty Hunters'' 4]]</ref>

==History==
{{Quote|Nexu are cats I actually like. Some people are scared of them. But to me they just have a few more eyes and teeth than usual.|[[Skora]]|<ref name="Hunters">''[[Star Wars: Hunters]]''</ref>}}
[[File:Seize_the_Day_Conv.png|thumb|right|250px|Poggle the Lesser attempted to use a nexu to kill Senator Padmé Amidala.]]
The nexu's fierce reputation made them popular animals for [[gladiator]] matches,<ref name="VE" /> making them a frequent target for [[Poaching|poachers]].<ref name="Nexu GoC" />

[[Archduke]] [[Poggle the Lesser]] kept a [[Unidentified nexu|nexu]] in the [[Petranaki Arena]] on [[Geonosis]]. The beast was used in the attempted execution of [[Senator]] [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] prior to the [[First Battle of Geonosis|outbreak]] of the [[Clone Wars]]. When a [[Geonosian]] guard attempted to direct the nexu with a blast from an electric pike, the creature became irritated and killed its provoker, tackling him off his mount and crushing his neck in its powerful jaws. It then found Senator Amidala, however, to be more difficult prey. Though it landed the first blow and slashed the senator across the back, injuring her, causing her to scream in pain, and ripping her outfit around her midriff and ripped off her sleeve, she returned the favor with a powerful kick which stunned the Nexu due to its weak skeletal structure; the predator was swiftly [[Death|killed]] soon afterwards by a [[reek]] ridden by [[Anakin Skywalker]], which rammed it head-on with its horn.<ref name="AotC" />

[[File:NexuStalksOmega-CaR.png|thumb|left|250px|A nexu stalks Omega outside the Lawquane's farm]]
[[Clone commando]] [[Tech]] of [[Clone Force 99]] had a recording of a nexu among his collection of many such creature sounds.<ref name="OTWOK">{{TCW|On the Wings of Keeradaks}}</ref> In [[19 BBY]],<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' places the events of [[The Bad Batch Season 1|''The Bad Batch'' Season 1]] in [[19 BBY]].</ref> a nexu approached the Lawquane farm and attempted to kill the young [[Gender|female]] clone [[Omega]] after she came out of the safe zone. [[Suu Lawquane]] shot the beast before it took action and it fled when the former [[Clone Sergeant]] [[Hunter (clone)|Hunter]] attacked it with a vibro [[knife]].<ref name="Cut and Run" />

[[Marg Krim]], the leader of the [[Pyke Syndicate]], owned a horde of nexus, which he threaten to feed [[Looti Vario]]'s remains to them, when the [[Aleena]] contacted him about the attack on his [[spice]] shipments on [[Janix]].<ref name="Chapter 3">{{MSL|Chapter 3: Whispers in the Unknown}}</ref>

At some point during the [[New Republic Era]], [[Neo-Imperialism|Neo-Imperial]] [[warlord]] [[Commander]] [[Janu Coin]] had the head of a nexu mounted on a wall in his [[Janu Coin's estate|estate]] on [[Shakari]].<ref name="Star Wars: The Mandalorian and Grogu">''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian and Grogu]]''</ref>

By the [[time]] of the [[First Order-Resistance War|war]] between the [[First Order]] and the [[Resistance]], the [[Ithorian]] storekeeper [[Dok-Ondar]] had the head of a nexu mounted on a wall in his store, [[Dok-Ondar's Den of Antiquities]], in [[Black Spire Outpost]] on the planet [[Batuu]].<ref name="Den of Antiquities">{{GalaxysEdge|Dok-Ondar's Den of Antiquities}}</ref>

The nexu's unsavory reputation prompted the saying "Look what the nexu dragged in" to become commonplace in certain reaches of the galaxy. One such user of the phrase was [[Wen Delphis]], leader of the [[Sixth Kin]], who uttered it when a past employ of hers, [[Just Lucky]], returned to her after a substantial time of absence.<ref name="DA">[[Doctor Aphra (2020) 7|''Doctor Aphra'' (2020) 7]]</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Nexu_Concept_Art.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Concept art by [[Robert E. Barnes]]]]
The nexu that appeared in [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Star Wars'': Episode II ''Attack of the Clones'']] was nicknamed "Bad Kitty" by the [[Industrial Light & Magic|ILM]] animation team.<ref name="EpGuide">{{SWArchive|url=theclonewars/guide/episode205.html|text=''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide: Landing at Point Rain}}</ref>

Robert Barnes designed the nexu; early concept sketches depicted a very [[Wikipedia:Lion|lionlike]] creature. The nexu's final design came about when Barnes mixed feline traits with those of other species, such as [[Wikipedia:Reptile|reptiles]] and humans.<ref name="DB-nexu">{{DB|creature|nexu|nexu}}</ref>

