{{Listen3|RaxshirRoar-LifeAndDeath.flac|a raxshir roaring|A raxshir roars at an infant Ahsoka Tano}}
'''Raxshir''', also referred to as '''sabertooths''', were a type of large, [[Diet|predatory]] [[feline]] with [[Color|yellow]] [[Hair|fur]] with black stripes. One raxshir lived in a [[pine]] [[forest]] on the [[planet]] [[Shili]] and attacked the [[Togruta]] [[Pav-ti Tano]] and [[Ahsoka Tano]] there in [[35 BBY]]. The creature took the [[Youngling|infant]] Ahsoka and fled when more Togruta arrived, carrying her by the scruff of her neck to a clearing in the forest. There, the child [[Force power|used]] [[the Force]] to [[Taming beasts|calm]] the raxshir and then rode on its back while they returned to her [[Ahsoka Tano's village|village]]. At the [[City|village]], the raxshir allowed Pav-ti to take Ahsoka from its back before leaving peacefully.

==Biology and appearance==
Raxshir,<ref name="CGttSWG" /> also known as sabertooths,<ref name="Audio Description" /> were a type of large,<ref name="CGttSWG" /> [[tiger]]-like<ref name="Audio Description" /> [[feline]] that measured four [[meter]]s (twelve [[Foot|feet]]) in length.<ref name="CGttSWG" /> Hulking and ferocious<ref name="SWI218">{{InsiderCite|218|Ahsoka So Far}}</ref> [[Diet|predators]],<ref name="StoryGallery" /> the [[Tooth|fanged]] animals<ref name="CGttSWG" /> had two large teeth protruding from the upper [[Mouth|jaw]] as well as a series of smaller teeth between them on both jaws. The felines had a flat, pink [[nose]] and a pair of glowing [[Color|golden]] [[eye]]s beneath a pair of [[ear]]s and a crest of black [[Hair|fur]], with the rest of their fur being yellow with black stripes on the upper side of their [[Limb|quadrupedal]] body and white on the underside. Each of their four paws had four [[claw]]ed toes and their tail was thick and nearly reached the ground.<ref name="Life and Death" />

==History==
===Forest feline===
{{Quote|No! No! Ahsoka!|Pav-ti cries out as the raxshir takes Ahsoka|audio=NoAhsoka-Pav-Ti-LifeAndDeath.flac|<ref name="Life and Death" />}}
[[File:RaxshirAttack-LifeAndDeath.png|thumb|right|300px|A raxshir attacked Pav-ti and Ahsoka Tano on Shili.]]
In [[35 BBY]],<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' establishes that [[Ahsoka Tano]] was [[Reproduction|born]] in [[36 BBY]]. As the scenes in "[[Life and Death]]" take place a [[Standard year|year]] after her birth, they must occur in [[35 BBY]].</ref> a raxshir [[Homeworld|lived]] in the<ref name="Life and Death" /> [[pine]]<ref name="Audio Description" /> [[forest]]s that surrounded a [[Togruta]] [[Ahsoka Tano's village|village]] on<ref name="Life and Death" /> the [[planet]] [[Shili]].<ref name="Audio Description" /> When the Togruta [[Parent|mother]] [[Pav-ti Tano]] traveled into the forest with<ref name="Life and Death" /> her<ref name="CGttSWG" /> [[Youngling|infant]] [[Tano family|daughter]], [[Ahsoka Tano]], to [[Hunting|hunt]] a [[kybuck]], the raxshir watched the pair while hidden in tall [[grass]] among the [[tree]]s. It crept up on the pair in a clearing where they had [[Death|killed]] a kybuck, with Ahsoka spotting the creature as it approached.<ref name="Life and Death" />

When Pav-ti also realized the creature was there, she slowly reached for her [[blaster rifle]] as the raxshir continued to move closer, with the feline growling at her before she could grab the weapon. The mother then stood and roared at the raxshir with her arms stretched wide to try and intimidate it, causing the feline to rear back and groan. However, as she grabbed the [[rifle]], it swiped at her several times as she dodged and rolled out of the way. The raxshir then got its jaws around the rifle and used it to throw Pav-ti across the clearing, growling at her again.<ref name="Life and Death" /> Showing no fear,<ref name="SWI218" /> Ahsoka then gurgled, drawing the ferocious feline's attention<ref name="Life and Death" /> and saving her [[Gender|mother's]] life.<ref name="SWI218" /> It charged at the infant but returned its attention to Pavi-ti when she opened fire with the rifle. After the raxshir disarmed her, she drew a [[knife]] and slashed at it, wounding one of the creature's legs while it tried to slash her with its claws repeatedly.<ref name="Life and Death" />

[[File:RaxshirCarryingAhsoka-LifeAndDeath.png|thumb|left|300px|The raxshir carried off Ahsoka Tano.]]
Rising on its hind legs, it finally knocked Pav-ti to the ground and then approached Ahsoka. By that point, other Togruta from the [[City|village]] had been drawn to the clearing by the sound of [[blaster]] fire and fired on the raxshir as it tried to grab Ahsoka. The creature roared at them, then managed to pick up the crying infant in its mouth before fleeing from the clearing.<ref name="Life and Death" />

===Subdued sabertooth===
{{Quote|I'm sorry, Nak-il. There's no sign of her or the creature.''"<br />"''We will go out in force. We will not stop until we find her.|A Togruta villager and Nak-il Tano|audio=FindAhsoka-Nak-il-LifeAndDeath.flac|<ref name="Life and Death" />}}
[[File:AhsokaTamesSabertooth-LaD.png|thumb|right|300px|Ahsoka Tano used the Force to calm the raxshir.]]
As dusk settled,<ref name="Audio Description" /> the raxshir carried Ahsoka through the forest by the scruff of her neck as the baby babbled,<ref name="Life and Death" /> seemingly unperturbed by the creature.<ref name="Audio Description" /> Upon reaching a clearing, the creature dropped her and began grooming its forepaw. When the infant sneezed, the raxshir roared at her, but Ahsoka cooed in response and stood, moving toward the feline. Watching her warily, the creature growled and licked its jaws before moving closer<ref name="Life and Death" /> to eat its prey.<ref name="StoryGallery" /> As it reached the child, Ahsoka placed her hand upon its nose<ref name="Life and Death" /> and instinctively [[Force power|used]] [[the Force]] to [[Taming beasts|calm]] the wild beast,<ref name="Ahsoka">{{SW|url=news/who-is-ahsoka-tano|text=Who Is Ahsoka Tano?}}</ref> causing it to stop.<ref name="Life and Death" />

The raxshir's eyes met with those of Ahsoka and it sat back on its haunches in front of her, roaring at her without breaking eye contact.<ref name="Life and Death" /> Meanwhile, the infant's parents and the other villagers aggressively hunted for the raxshir, fearing that it would harm Ahsoka,<ref name="SWI225">{{InsiderCite|225|Children of the Galaxy (article)}}</ref> but found no sign of the creature or child.<ref name="Life and Death" /> With the [[Force-sensitive]] infant able to communicate with the raxshir through the Force,<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|ahsoka-tano|Ahsoka Tano}}</ref> the feline gingerly<ref name="Top10">{{SW|url=news/ahsoka-tano-greatest-moments|text=10 of Ahsoka Tano's Greatest Moments}}</ref> returned Ahsoka to the village that [[Local day|night]]. As the pair arrived, Ahsoka's father, [[Nak-il Tano]], was preparing to lead another group out to search for his daughter. Hearing the raxshir's roars as it approached, Pav-ti stepped toward the edge of the forest as it emerged, while the other villagers aimed their weapons. The raxshir roared, but did not attack, and the Togruta [[Gantika]] ordered the villagers to hold their fire.<ref name="Life and Death" />

[[File:AhsokaReturn-LifeAndDeath.png|thumb|left|300px|The subdued raxshir returned Ahsoka Tano to her village.]]
A smiling Ahsoka then became visible on the raxshir's back as it entered the light from the village, where the creature stopped before Pav-ti and lowered its head so that the mother could step forward and take the infant from<ref name="Life and Death" /> the subdued<ref name="Audio Description" /> feline's back. Rising back up<ref name="Life and Death" /> in a regal pose,<ref name="Audio Description" /> the creature gazed into Ahsoka's eyes once more as Pav-ti spoke to it in [[Togruti]], then the raxshir turned and left the village.<ref name="Life and Death" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:RaxshirStoryboard.png|thumb|right|200px|Justin Bruce Lee created storyboards of the raxshir.]]
A raxshir first appeared in "[[Life and Death]]," the first episode of the television series [[Star Wars: Tales of the Jedi (television series)|''Star Wars: Tales of the Jedi'']],<ref name="Life and Death" /> which first aired at [[Celebration Anaheim (2022)|''Star Wars'' Celebration Anaheim]] on [[May 28]], [[2022]],<ref name="io9">{{WebCite|url=https://gizmodo.com/star-wars-tales-of-the-jedi-lucasfilm-anthology-series-1848974981|text=Ahsoka, Qui-Gon & Count Dooku Return in New Anthology Series, ''Tales of the Jedi''|author=Carter, Justin|date=2022-05-28|archivedate=20220529061105}}</ref> before being released on [[Disney+]] on [[October 26]], 2022.<ref name="Trailer">{{SWYouTube|-uRRKqQbmw4|Tales Of The Jedi &#124; Official Trailer &#124; Disney Plus|sw_url=video/tales-of-the-jedi-official-trailer-disney}}</ref> Associate storyboard artist<ref name="Life and Death" /> [[Justin Bruce Lee]] created storyboards of the raxshir fighting Pav-ti Tano for the episode.<ref name="Twitter">{{Twitter|username=justbleeve|url=status/1585334380460810240|name=[[Justin Bruce Lee]]|date=2022-10-26|quote=Tales of the Jedi is finally out on @disneyplus!So thankful to learn under my episodic director @natenewton and master Dave filoni. Also very thankful to my whole team for inspiring me every day!}}</ref>

The episode's audio description refers to the creature only as a sabertooth,<ref name="Audio Description" /> but it was then identified as a raxshir in the [[StarWars.com]] Story Gallery for "Life and Death."<ref name="StoryGallery" /> The audio description also erroneously describes the raxshir as bringing Ahsoka to a cave<ref name="Audio Description" /> while the episode shows only a clearing.<ref name="Life and Death" />

