'''Reeks''' were large, muscular quadrupeds native to the [[planet]] [[Ylesia]]<ref name="SWJB" /> that could also be found on [[Saleucami]] and the [[Codian Moon]].<ref name="Bestiary" />

==Biology and appearance==
{{Quote|He could tear the horns off a reek with his bare hands.|[[Han Solo]], on [[Grakkus Jahibakti Tingi]]|<ref name="Star Wars (2015) 35">[[Star Wars (2015) 35|''Star Wars'' (2015) 35]]</ref>}}
Reeks were powerful and territorial [[mammal]]s with a single central horn atop their head and a cheek horn on either side. They lived on [[grass]] plains and turf and had powerful hind [[limb]]s for charging.<ref name="VE" /> According to the [[Mandalorian]] [[Aran Tal]], the creatures had an overwhelming smell.<ref name="Hunters">''[[Star Wars: Hunters]]''</ref>

Though naturally herbivores, a starved reek could become a ravenous meat-eater and change its skin color to a deep [[Color|red]], while on other worlds they could be brown, gray, or sometimes yellow. Those bred in the [[Petranaki Arena]] were purposely fed meat in order to increase their overall aggression,<ref name="AbEverything">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> and were equipped with nose rings to be used by handlers.<ref name="VE" /> Their sprawling posture and immense weight made them relatively slow-moving. They sported two large cheek horns that could be used for head-locking in combat with another reek as a show of dominance within a herd; these fights could end in the death of one of the reeks.<ref name="Bestiary" />

Reeks from the Codian [[Moon]] lived in small herds.<ref name="UFC">''[[Ultimate Factivity Collection: Star Wars]]''</ref>  

==Reeks in the galaxy==
[[File:Reek.jpg|thumb|left|250x250px|The Reek in the Petranaki arena on Geonosis.]]
[[Unidentified reek|A reek]] was used in the attempted execution of [[Anakin Skywalker]] in the Petranaki Arena on [[Geonosis]] just prior to the [[Clone Wars]].  Anakin, however, tamed the creature with [[the Force]] and broke his chains before directing it against a [[nexu]] attacking [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]], killing the smaller predator. The reek then separated from the [[Jedi]] when a [[First Battle of Geonosis|battle]] erupted in the arena, destroying [[battle droid]]s with impunity and losing one of its cheek horns to [[Mace Windu]] before attacking [[Jango Fett]]. Though Fett avoided being trampled by the creature and killed it with a single expertly aimed shot to the [[eye]], with his [[WESTAR-34 blaster pistol]]. However the reek damaged his [[JT-12 jetpack]], which Fett was unaware of and attempting to use the damaged [[jetpack]] led to his own [[death]] moments later by [[Mace Windu's lightsaber|Windu's blade]].<ref name="Episode II" />

The creatures existed on Saleucami as well, where one was ridden by [[General]] [[Grievous]], leader of the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] [[Separatist Droid Army|Droid Army]], during the [[battle of Saleucami]].<ref name="The Deserter">{{TCW|The Deserter}}</ref>

[[Garnac's hunting guild]] killed a reek and placed its head in their [[Ubrikkian Floating Fortress]], alongside the trophies made of other [[Species|creatures]].<ref name="Wookiee Hunt">{{TCW|Wookiee Hunt}}</ref>

At some point during the [[New Republic Era]], [[Neo-Imperialism|Neo-Imperial]] [[warlord]] [[Janu Coin]] had the head of a reek mounted on a wall in his [[Janu Coin's estate|estate]] on [[Shakari]].<ref name="Star Wars: The Mandalorian and Grogu">''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian and Grogu]]''</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Reeks first appeared in [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Star Wars'': Episode II ''Attack of the Clones'']].<ref name="Episode II" />

There is a discrepancy regarding the creature's height. Both the [[Encyclopedia (StarWars.com)|Encyclopedia]] and [[Memory bank/Legends|Databank]] entries agree that these creatures stood at about 2.24 meters tall. However, the later ''[[Star Wars Journeys: Beginnings]]'' claims that they stood at 4.04 meters in height. As 4.04 meters is the listed length of reeks in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, however, ''Beginnings'' may have mistakenly listed the creature's length as its height.

