{{Quote|I was barely walking when I learned to ride thrantas. From the best, I might add.|Princess Leia Organa|<ref name="FoD">''[[Forces of Destiny—Leia]]''</ref>}}
'''Thrantas''' were a large, flying [[species]] native to the [[planet]] [[Alderaan]]. As a species, they survived the [[Destruction of Alderaan|destruction]] of their [[homeworld]] due to the relocation of some thrantas to [[Bespin]].

==Biology and appearance==
Thrantas were [[Color|gray]]-skinned floating beasts with broad triangular wings and a long tail that served as a stabilizer during flight.<ref name="Bestiary" /> They greatly resembled<ref name="Leia 2" /> the [[aiwha]], a [[species]] of winged [[cetacean]]s [[Homeworld|native]] to [[Kamino]].<ref name="Aiwha">{{Databank|aiwha|Aiwha}}</ref> They emitted mournful cries as they flew.<ref name="Eclipse">{{StoryCite|story=Eclipse (short story)|book=From a Certain Point of View}}</ref>

==Behavior==
Thrantas were migratory creatures who lived in social groupings referred to as "herds"<ref name="Eclipse" /> or "flocks".<ref name="Princess of Alderaan">''[[Leia, Princess of Alderaan]]''</ref>

==History==
Thrantas hailed from the [[planet]] [[Alderaan]], one of the so-called [[Core Worlds]] of [[the galaxy]]. As she grew up as a [[Prince|crown princess]] in the [[House of Organa]], [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] notably learned to ride a thranta.<ref name="Backstories">''[[Princess Leia: Royal Rebel]]''</ref> Although Alderaan was [[Destruction of Alderaan|destroyed]] by the [[Galactic Empire]]<ref name="Episode IV">{{Film|IV}}</ref> in [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas: Updated Edition]]''</ref> the species outlived its homeworld as a population had been transplanted to the [[gas giant]] [[Bespin]]. Those Bespinian thrantas lived in a breathable [[Life Zone|region]] of the planet's [[atmosphere]], where they were ridden through the clouds by only the most daring thrill seekers.<ref name="USW" />

==Behind the scenes==
Thranta first appeared in concept art drawn by artist [[Ralph McQuarrie]] for [[Star Wars: Episode V The Empire Strikes Back|''Star Wars'': Episode V ''The Empire Strikes Back'']],<ref name="Making of ESB">''[[The Making of The Empire Strikes Back]]''</ref> which was later reused in ''[[The Illustrated Star Wars Universe]]'' in [[1995]], introducing them to the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity.<ref name="ISWU">''[[The Illustrated Star Wars Universe]]''</ref> The species was made [[canon]] by the reference book ''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]'', which was released in [[2015]].<ref name="USW" />

