'''Veermoks''' were a wild [[species]] of clawed and sharp-toothed [[primate]]s native to the [[planet]] [[Naboo]]. A distinct [[Eriadu veermok|subspecies]] lived on planet [[Eriadu]], in the [[Outer Rim Territories]]. They could also be found on the planet [[Xirl]].

==Biology and appearance==
Veermoks were a [[Sentience|non-sentient]] [[species]] of [[Diet|carnivorous]] [[primate]]s<ref name="Tarkin" /> that possessed a broad upper torso, long and powerful [[Limb|arms]], but comparatively thin hind limbs. They had three-fingered paws tipped in jagged white claws,<ref name="The Nest" /> and a [[dog]]-like muzzle containing razor-sharp [[Tooth|teeth]].<ref name="Tarkin" /> Their back and arms were covered in wooly, [[Color|dark brown]] [[Hair|fur]],<ref name="The Nest" /> but their lower anatomy was hairless. A single specimen had the strength of ten humans.<ref name="Tarkin" />

==Behavior==
{{Quote|Are they aggressive?''"<br />"''Very.|Lina and Milo Graf|<ref name="The Nest" />}}
Living in [[swamp]]s and damp woodlands, veermoks were [[Tree|arboreal]] creatures. They were also lonely creatures, spending most of their lives without others of their kind,<ref name="Tarkin" /> and highly aggressive.<ref name="The Nest" />

==History==
Veermoks evolved on [[Naboo]],<ref name="The Nest" /> a bountiful [[planet]] situated in the [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim]] region of [[the galaxy]].<ref name="Ultimate SW">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref>

==Veermoks in the galaxy==
A very distinct [[Eriadu veermok|subspecies]] lived on [[Eriadu]], a world of the [[Outer Rim Territories]] that was practically galactic neighbors with Naboo. That subspecies differred from the more ordinary veermok both in appearance and social behavior.<ref name="Tarkin" />

